Language    : Python 3

Description
-----------
This module introduces Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)
in Python.

Object-Oriented Programming is a programming paradigm
that organizes software using classes and objects.
It allows developers to model real-world entities,
improve code organization, encourage code reuse,
and simplify software maintenance.

Learning Objectives
-------------------
1. Understand classes and objects.
2. Create a class.
3. Define attributes.
4. Define methods.
5. Instantiate objects.
6. Call object methods.
7. Display object information.

Functions Used
--------------
print()         Display information.
__init__()      Initialize object attributes.

Expected Output
---------------
The program demonstrates how to define a class,
create an object, initialize attributes, and call
methods to display object information.

Coding Style
------------
This module follows clean code principles and PEP 8
recommendations for readability, maintainability,
and professional software development.
=========================================================
"""


class Employee:
    """
    Represents an employee.
    """

    def __init__(
        self,
        employee_id,
        name,
        department,
        country
    ):
        """Initialize employee attributes."""

        self.employee_id = employee_id
        self.name = name
        self.department = department
        self.country = country

    def display_information(self):
        """Display employee information."""

        print()
        print("Employee Information")
        print("-" * 70)
        print(f"Employee ID : {self.employee_id}")
        print(f"Name        : {self.name}")
        print(f"Department  : {self.department}")
        print(f"Country     : {self.country}")


def display_header():
    """Display the program title."""

    print("=" * 70)
    print("Python Object-Oriented Programming")
    print("=" * 70)


def main():
    """Main entry point of the program."""

    display_header()

    employee = Employee(
        employee_id=1001,
        name="Kushendar",
        department="Cyber Security",
        country="Indonesia"
    )

    employee.display_information()

    print()
    print("=" * 70)
    print("Program Completed Successfully")
    print("=" * 70)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
